---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {url,nevermore} from '../lib/catalogue';
---
<Layout title="Credits, Rights & Privacy | GlassPlay" description="Credits, privacy and release rights for GlassPlay and Nevermore. Clear separation of code, artwork, third-party components and device validation." path="credits/">
  <article class="reading-page wrap"><h1>Made with care.<br /><em>Shared with clarity.</em></h1>
    <section id="glassplay"><h2>GlassPlay</h2><p>An independent collection by RBraga01. The website uses Astro, Manrope and Newsreader. The fonts are self-hosted under the SIL Open Font License; the website artwork and branding are original project work.</p><p>The glasses image is original conceptual artwork, not a hardware product photograph. Christmas, Easter and St. Patrick's Day are future concepts, not finished applications.</p><p><a href={url('licenses/Manrope-OFL.txt')}>Manrope font license</a> · <a href={url('licenses/Newsreader-OFL.txt')}>Newsreader font license</a></p></section>
    <section id="nevermore"><h2>Nevermore</h2><p>Nevermore's character artwork was developed using 3D assets created with Meshy and animated for this project. Only finished rendered visuals are presented; original source models are not distributed.</p><p>Production audio combines real recordings with individual CC0 provenance, original edits and generated Guardian voices. Their source credits are retained in the candidate's CREDITS.json; CC0 source recordings do not make the complete soundtrack or artwork CC0.</p><p>The offline Vosk speech model carries its Apache-2.0 license. Raven Framework is a separate dependency from Raven Resonance; it is not included or relicensed by Nevermore.</p><p>Nevermore's code is MIT-licensed. Its artwork, rendered media and soundtrack are All Rights Reserved; underlying CC0 recordings keep CC0. This website presents an independent project; the application is not yet available for public download.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Honest previews</h2><p>Nevermore {nevermore.candidate!.version} has Windows-host and Raven Simulator validation. Physical Prism testing is still pending. Production-animation stills are rendered assets; any Simulator footage is labelled. Neither is presented as footage from physical glasses.</p></section>
    <section id="privacy"><h2>Privacy</h2><p>This static website uses no analytics, advertising, third-party embeds, forms, cookies or local storage. Fonts and available media are served with the site. The hosting provider may process ordinary access logs; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p><p>Inside Nevermore, recognition is local and foreground-only, active while armed and idle. Normal operation does not save microphone recordings. Discoveries are stored locally and can be reset. No account or cloud profile is required.</p></section>
    <a class="text-link" href={url('experiences/nevermore/')}>Back to Nevermore</a>
  </article>
</Layout>
